! Cl ATOM | EXTERNAL BASIS FILE TEST (EXTFIL, not BASNAM)
!
! ============================================================
! Why this file exists
! ============================================================
! caa005b-cl-atom-basischeck.inp (same molecule/geometry/basis DATA, but
! using inline $BASIS BASNAM(1)=clbas $END with the basis defined directly
! in the .inp after $DATA) crashed with:
!   ** On entry to DGEMM  parameter number 13 had an illegal value
! immediately after ONE-ELECTRON INTEGRALS, before any SCF iteration.
!
! This tests whether GAMESS's OTHER custom-basis mechanism -- EXTFIL,
! reading basis sets from a separate external file via the EXTBAS
! environment variable, keyed by chemical symbol rather than atom position
! -- exercises a different internal code path that avoids the crash.
!
! Everything else (molecule: isolated Cl atom, UHF, MULT=2, geometry, SCF
! settings) is unchanged from caa005b-cl-atom-basischeck.inp. The basis
! DATA itself is byte-for-byte identical (verified by diff against the
! working def2-TZVPP source) -- only the MECHANISM by which GAMESS reads it
! has changed, from inline BASNAM to external EXTFIL.
!
! Requires: environment variable EXTBAS set to point to def2tzvp_ext.bas
! before rungms is called (confirmed rungms itself does not set/reset
! EXTBAS at all, so exporting it beforehand should reach the GAMESS binary
! unmodified).

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=UHF RUNTYP=ENERGY DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         MULT=2 ICHARG=0 NOSYM=1 MAXIT=200
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS GBASIS=DEF2TZVP EXTFIL=.TRUE. $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=20 MEMDDI=20 $END

 $DATA
Isolated chlorine atom -- EXTFIL external basis test
C1
Cl   17.0   0.0   0.0   0.0
 $END
